adjudication.rationale:
In `apps/web/pages/api/webhook/app-credential.ts`, the webhook auth check directly compares a user-controlled request header to `process.env.CALCOM_WEBHOOK_SECRET` using `!==`:

```ts
if (
  req.headers[process.env.CALCOM_WEBHOOK_HEADER_NAME || "calcom-webhook-secret"] !==
  process.env.CALCOM_WEBHOOK_SECRET
) {
  return res.status(403)...
}
```

JavaScript string equality/inequality is not constant-time and can short-circuit (e.g., length check / first differing character), so this introduces a measurable timing side-channel in principle. A safer pattern would use `crypto.timingSafeEqual` on normalized `Buffer`s (and also handle `string | string[] | undefined`).
